  "description": "XIVYUX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H134 N52 O58 Pr6 8+,3(H3 O1 1+),11(Cl1 1-),29(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr1B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3B (Pr) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.783-3.979 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.82-109.99°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H201Cl11N52O90Pr6.",
